{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.050215Z","id":"a4f990641be5e86a6ba0430d37a89aa4303a9af7e3ef1afb3f5b26e26670ef38","body":{"detail":"price_the_web sets the web lines, so cost_milli in steps.web.json, journal.web.json, events.web.json and audit.web.json is the tests' own (50 and 100). What a turn is charged is still the seeded price of claude-sonnet-5-5: `credits_milli` 1931 and 931 in events.*.json and audit.*.json, and through it `left.credits` in script.web-operations.json, script.web-refusals.json, steps.web.json, journal.web.json and resumed.rebase-publish-fetch.json (1997.919 is the weekly 2000 less a turn's 1.931, a search and a fetch). A change to that model's seeded token price rewrites those goldens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"7c1dc2bb29598804dcd02ecf8d65232e74e43f07a76548cd2d72c8659c039195"},"suggested_fix":"Set the model's four token lines in Env::new (tests/common/mod.rs) or give the runs a model priced by the test, and regenerate.","summary":"The goldens still hold the store's seeded token prices: only what a search and a fetch cost is set by the tests","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:15:22.050281Z","id":"fb9b407b008e3c62cfd61b37847758910e3c4c2f69233667ae4bc0cbf7ab9e61","body":{"detail":"Pins::events drains a Subscription made before the run's first tick, so every event it gets was emitted live. EventHub::subscribe rebuilds the committed steps' events from the store (crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs, canonical): `call` events from a step's stored `calls`, `step_done` from its payload. A change there (a `call` without cost_milli or web, a step_done without its summary) fails no golden of crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":435},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"d67eceda21f8932148845518e42c8b916c1f18b872ddc42e22ad087e416485cb"},"suggested_fix":"Subscribe again after the run ended and pin the replay beside the live events, or assert the two are equal but for turn_delta.","summary":"events.*.json pin the live events alone: what a subscriber that connects late is replayed (events::canonical) has no golden","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T04:21:20.133810Z","id":"b6143a74bb31aa6df7015d9385d0b87ecc045a7e801e7b93422975b4cf6354ba","body":{"detail":"price_the_web sets the web lines, so cost_milli in steps.web.json, journal.web.json, events.web.json and audit.web.json is the tests' own (50 and 100). What a turn is charged is still the seeded price of claude-sonnet-5-5: `credits_milli` 1931 and 931 in events.*.json and audit.*.json, and through it `left.credits` in script.web-operations.json, script.web-refusals.json, steps.web.json, journal.web.json and resumed.rebase-publish-fetch.json (1997.919 is the weekly 2000 less a turn's 1.931, a search and a fetch). A change to that model's seeded token price rewrites those goldens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"420d5a296bd048351a8614f70cc45ab4afc8c5e0ecf7542788d13eaeed130f71"},"suggested_fix":"Set the model's four token lines in Env::new (tests/common/mod.rs) or give the runs a model priced by the test, and regenerate.","summary":"The goldens still hold the store's seeded token prices: only what a search and a fetch cost is set by the tests","supersedes":"a4f990641be5e86a6ba0430d37a89aa4303a9af7e3ef1afb3f5b26e26670ef38","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111506Z","id":"6782082480035606710846c39fb8faebb967d53b0882c7c9f0fc079616fd1179","body":{"detail":"Pins::ending lists the replies grouped by thread (Env::replies reads thread 1, then thread 2) and the notices' journal places without their thread. In crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1515, `self.run.thread_ids.iter().rev().enumerate()` (thread 2 posted first, at NOTICE_SEQ) and `.iter().enumerate().rev()` (thread 2 posted first, at NOTICE_SEQ + 1) both pass, the six two-thread ending goldens included (ending.give-up.two-threads.json, ending.stopped.run-cap.two-threads.json, ending.failed.two-threads.json and the three finish ones). Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. The close fbe7b6d046b09fbc49d9e26765382acddec15ebe8fcef5725d2b66fbd9172441 covers which threads get a notice, not this.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record d17b70df on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":567},"end":{"line":592},"content_hash":"499dc66d904a339d10895460175712f54a2a86ec2e4f0592403c57b71c1cf19d"},"suggested_fix":"Add to Pins::ending the fake host's committed reply writes in order (FakeState::writes, crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs:322-326: key, thread), or map each notice's journal entry to its thread.","summary":"An ending golden does not say which thread a notice went to or in what order they were posted: reversing the threads in notify_at passes the suite","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111565Z","id":"40a0a4fb074ad23d22389bf806eabeb88c5a9852db25b0f8ff19f4caa9d130c4","body":{"detail":"Moving `self.deps.host.working(&self.run, false).await` to before `self.commit` in give_up (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1727-1738) or in finish (run.rs:1707-1717) passes the suite. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. The order is behaviour: the server's working(false) starts the follow-ups only for a run that is terminal (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs:1041-1067, crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs:983-992). With the finish change, `bazel test --test_arg=follow_up //crates/clax-server:integration__6` fails api_claxbot_run::comments_on_a_claxbot_thread_follow_up_on_their_authors_credits_and_rights (tests/api_claxbot_run.rs:565, `the condition held: Elapsed(())`, after 120 s; it passes in 1.4 s unchanged), so the order is held there alone, and slowly. The count of `true` is one per tick that reaches a turn or a script, attempts that fail to commit included (ending.failed.*.json hold three): each renews the 120 s working record (crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:12, 434).\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 9655610a on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":591},"content_hash":"d7816e72d051f2064ccac455fa1401a74af11beecbc9b32d647d884486923464"},"suggested_fix":"Have the fake host record with each working call whether the run was terminal in the store (or the run's status), and pin that in the roster.","summary":"The roster is a flat list of working calls, so no golden tells working(false) after the terminal commit from working(false) before it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/endings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111618Z","id":"87978c02cf8aa94052afca893880940b5b84e21d342aa09f9bd4ce799fbeaca5","body":{"detail":"(1) In finish (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1687-1689), posting `{summary}{list}` on the first thread only passes the suite: finish.no-reply.sources and finish.no-reply.three-sources are runs of one thread, and finish.no-reply.two-threads fetched nothing. (2) In History::of (run.rs:629-630), `wrote` without `|| !p[\"published\"].is_null()` passes the suite: no run replies, then publishes from a script that changes no file (edits in one script, the reply in the next, the publish in a third). The `changed` half is held: without it ending.finish.replied-before-a-draft-write.json fails at `\"posted\"`. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record a71508ec on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"68a66adb55487774e2affc36fdc17f30244bfffbd5a38a61baa2ac98aef0ac70"},"suggested_fix":"fetched_then(\"\", true) pinned as finish.no-reply.two-threads.sources; and a run of three scripts (edit; reply; publish) pinned as finish.replied-before-a-publish.","summary":"Two halves of the finish rule have no golden: a summary with sources on a run of two threads that did not reply, and a reply made before a script that published without editing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/answers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111657Z","id":"6be255db7f6ed86f34f243aa5124147636c0ac1d6bfdedaa536b1585d4c59c5e","body":{"detail":"`push` (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:568-576) merges a message into the last one of the same role; the one case in a run is the assistant turn after a pause_turn. pin_answer pins the second request, which holds the paused turn alone; the merged message would be in a third. With the merged blocks put first (`m.content.splice(0..0, content)` at run.rs:573) the suite passes. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. With no merging at all only the unit test run::tests::history_merges_consecutive_turns_of_one_role fails, no golden.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 1d7d88c8 on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"5d69c3c63340e5e2da5a1114862f7ccb496060693c4d895c1a24de0d92c412b2"},"suggested_fix":"A run of a paused turn, a turn with no tool call and a finish, pinning the third request's messages.","summary":"No pinned request holds two turns of one role merged: answer.pause-turn.json is the request after the paused turn, before the turn that continues it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/scripts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111699Z","id":"0178e69f71621ba369f0dac7b18ef0fc91c14da3dd1c5f4787a071ad2b039eb7","body":{"detail":"journal.thread.json, journal.web.json and steps.{thread,brief,web}.json hold only files.read, files.replace, draft.check, draft.publish, threads.reply and the web operations. the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned, a_publish_conflict_and_the_rebase_after_it_are_pinned and a_second_artifact_is_refused pin the tool result alone (script_result), whose calls carry op, ok and code. Passing changes, in crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs: files.write not journaled (line 392: `replay.is_none() && op != \"files.write\"`); draft.rebase journaled without its value (line 393, `false`), which a rebase made again reads its version from (lines 240-253); a refused publish not journaled (lines 399-401 removed); a rules refusal not journaled (lines 373-375 removed); and in crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs:739-753 the target of draft.rebase, or of files.write, made None. Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 8edda3bc on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"1d60e474d4a013708fc07ff1bafd7892512772a2746e7dde215965fbebef7454"},"suggested_fix":"Pin Pins::journal and the script step's `calls` for the draft-operations run and the rebase run (journal.draft-operations.json, journal.draft-rebase.json, or one golden each with result, calls and journal).","summary":"The journal rows and step `calls` of the draft-operations and rebase scripts are not pinned: six changes to what is journaled or to a call's target pass the suite","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/scripts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111727Z","id":"72b0381790a091e5e40e0012b5862eed6d435113260d2e6ed5678ed4ed1ec107","body":{"detail":"a_replay_that_diverged_is_pinned is the only golden of a script run again, and it diverges at call 0. In RunHost::publish (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs:289-298), removing `st.draft.base_version = p.version;` and `st.moved = true;` from the replay branch passes the suite, tests/resume.rs and tests/replay.rs included, though the step's `base` is then not recorded after a crash between a publish and the step's commit (History::of reads it at crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:598-600, and the next script loads its draft from it at script.rs:552-553). Each change was made alone at 2948421c4 and reverted; `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all` with the flags of scripts/lib/bazel-test-flags.sh then reported clax_bot_lib_test and integration PASSED. The same lines on the first run are held (steps.thread.json and steps.brief.json line 55, `\"base\": 2`).\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 7c5dd6f4 on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":256},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"4fe942bbecbaed658974097aefaa2b36495bae0783ee04ae63c6f5696949124c"},"suggested_fix":"A run whose script publishes, crashed before the step commits (tests/resume.rs crashed_run), resumed: pin the step's payload and the journal across the crash.","summary":"A publish answered from the journal is not pinned: a replayed publish that leaves the draft's base where it was passes the suite","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111765Z","id":"8d7a8b6160db76b3a7fe67861871806bee4c3dd3c2286bd6a66aae888c0d26da","body":{"detail":"The goldens script.web-operations.json and script.web-refusals.json hold every message script/web.rs and src/web/url.rs word themselves. Not pinned, by reading: (1) the errors web.rs passes on from the store through host_error (WebAccess::now, bot_web_counts, bot_web_calls, web_pages, rate_of, one_request, week_usage, flags_of, the journal entry and spend_journaled; web.rs lines 504, 559, 573, 650, 750-794, 830): the tests' store is the real one and has no way to fail one read in the middle of a script; (2) `the host is a private or local address` (url.rs:100), which no http or https URL reaches, since url::Url refuses one without a host first; (3) the words a source answers itself: FakeWebSource's (src/web/fake.rs: a redirect from https to http, a redirect chain past the limit, a redirect to no URL) are the fake's, and the daemon's and the Worker's sources word their own outside this crate; (4) `clax.<op> is not available to this run` is driven by a run that did not declare the operation, not by a host without a source (Deps::web None), which answers the same words.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 49ba7270 on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":463},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"66aa3e97ec845d8f84b737478ba5ca2eb53e473d046e1e786a4fda988bc1255d"},"suggested_fix":"If script/web.rs moves behind a session that can fail a read, pin one store error's passage then; pin the real sources' redirect and timeout words in the crates that hold them.","summary":"What a script can be told by crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs that no golden pins: a store error passed through as it is, and a fake source's own words","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.111804Z","id":"200e9fe4ddff05abac226807de4aad3cbfd9240ccabfc95eb35f22169707c5df","body":{"detail":"`named` strips `ending.`, `script.` or `answer.` and `.json` and looks for the rest as `\"stem\"` anywhere in the code, so a file is named by a string of another prefix (`\"pause-turn\"` names ending.pause-turn.json and script.pause-turn.json as well as answer.pause-turn.json) or by any literal equal to its stem (`\"done\"`, `\"fetch\"`, `\"Edit\"`), and by a pin in a test that is `#[ignore]`d or not compiled. A pin whose name is built (`format!`) or lives in another module reports its goldens as unnamed, which fails loudly; splitting this file breaks the check until it reads every part.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 28ac5e85 on crates/clax-bot/tests/golden.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":193},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"32a82028fe00f9473f027f6db9ad205ef4e17231e1f65b67ec657cb9652457fa"},"suggested_fix":"Name every golden through one function that takes the file name and records it (or a const table of names the pins index), and compare that set with the directory.","summary":"every_golden_is_named_by_a_pin reads this file's text: any string that ends with a golden's stem names it, and a pin moved to another file names nothing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/pins.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.112506Z","id":"a3ed4f5117e671c47bac909dac846e0492154d1d48ce0675bab08a76c7dbb06e","body":{"detail":"Pins::events drains a Subscription made before the run's first tick, so every event it gets was emitted live. EventHub::subscribe rebuilds the committed steps' events from the store (crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs, canonical): `call` events from a step's stored `calls`, `step_done` from its payload. A change there (a `call` without cost_milli or web, a step_done without its summary) fails no golden of crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":483},"end":{"line":516},"content_hash":"d67eceda21f8932148845518e42c8b916c1f18b872ddc42e22ad087e416485cb"},"suggested_fix":"Subscribe again after the run ended and pin the replay beside the live events, or assert the two are equal but for turn_delta.","summary":"events.*.json pin the live events alone: what a subscriber that connects late is replayed (events::canonical) has no golden","supersedes":"fb9b407b008e3c62cfd61b37847758910e3c4c2f69233667ae4bc0cbf7ab9e61","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
